<.shell title="Tables" current={:tables}>
  <h1>Tables</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    32px rows by default, 24px when compact. Cells line up on their first line of text, so a
    row with a wrapped cell still reads across.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Text at sm (14px). Headers semibold on <code>--surface-alt</code>, and they stick on scroll.
    </li>
    <li>Numbers right-aligned with tabular figures. Codes, such as letter numbers, in mono.</li>
    <li>
      Sortable headers show an arrow, or ⇅ when the column sorts both ways. The sorted column is
      underlined in primary and has <code>aria-sort</code>.
    </li>
    <li>Actions in a row are small buttons or links.</li>
    <li>
      Columns go in order of use: what identifies the row first, then what people act on, then
      the rest. IDs and contact details go last.
    </li>
    <li>
      On a phone, tables scroll sideways rather than reflow. When the first column names the row,
      it stays pinned while the rest scrolls.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Tax credit letters</h2>
  <form class="filter-bar" onsubmit="return false">
    <div class="field">
      <label for="year">Year</label>
      <select id="year" name="year"><option>2025</option><option>2024</option></select>
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <label for="q">Search</label>
      <input id="q" type="search" name="q" />
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <label for="hours">Hours</label>
      <select id="hours" name="hours">
        <option>200 hours or more</option>
        <option>Everyone</option>
      </select>
    </div>
  </form>
  <div class="table-summary">
    <a href="#">Reset filters</a>
    <span>{length(letters())} members</span>
  </div>
  <.table
    id="sample-letters"
    rows={letters()}
    class="table-striped"
    sort="total"
    path_fn={fn _ -> "#" end}
  >
    <:header_row>
      <th></th>
      <th colspan="3">SARVAC hours</th>
      <th colspan="3"></th>
    </:header_row>
    <:col :let={r} label="Name" class="whitespace-nowrap" sorts={[{"↑", "name"}]}>
      <a href="#" class="link">{r.name}</a>
    </:col>
    <:col :let={r} label="Primary" align="right" sorts={[{"↓", "primary"}]}>{r.primary}</:col>
    <:col :let={r} label="Secondary" align="right" sorts={[{"↓", "secondary"}]}>
      {r.secondary}
    </:col>
    <:col :let={r} label="Total" align="right" sorts={[{"↓", "total"}]}>
      <strong>{r.total}</strong>
    </:col>
    <:col :let={r} label="Letter" class="w-px">
      <a :if={r.letter} href="#" class="link mono">{r.letter}</a>
      <.button :if={!r.letter} variant={:success} size={:sm}>Create letter</.button>
    </:col>
    <:col :let={r} label="Email">{r.email}</:col>
    <:col :let={r} label="ID" class="w-px" align="right" sorts={[{"↑", "id"}]}>{r.id}</:col>
  </.table>
  <p class="spec">
    In the app:
    <code>&lt;.table id="…" rows=&#123;…&#125; sort=&#123;@sort&#125; path_fn=&#123;@path_fn&#125;&gt;</code>
    with a <code>&lt;:col label="…" sorts=&#123;[&#123;"↓", "total"&#125;]&#125;&gt;</code>
    for each column. A column that sorts both ways lists 2 sorts, such as <code>[&#123;"↓", "date-"&#125;, &#123;"↑", "date"&#125;]</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Attendance recommendations</h2>
  <p>Check the changes to make, then perform them.</p>
  <form onsubmit="return false">
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th class="shrink"><input type="checkbox" checked aria-label="All" /></th>
            <th class="shrink">Change</th>
            <th>Name</th>
            <th>Email</th>
            <th>Phone</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr :for={r <- recommendations()}>
            <td>
              <input :if={r.op != :not_invited} type="checkbox" checked aria-label={r.name} />
            </td>
            <td>
              <span :if={r.op == :add} class="op-add">Add</span>
              <span :if={r.op == :remove} class="op-remove">Remove</span>
              <span :if={r.op == :not_invited} class="tag danger">Not signed up</span>
            </td>
            <td>{r.name}</td>
            <td>{r.email}</td>
            <td>{r.phone}</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="actions">
      <button class="btn success">Perform 3 changes</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn secondary">Reset</button>
    </div>
  </form>

  <h2>Rule preview, with wrapping cells</h2>
  <p>Long text wraps; the other cells stay on its first line.</p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="striped pin-first">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Member</th>
          <th>Why</th>
          <th class="shrink"></th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr :for={{name, why, detail, days} <- rule_preview()}>
          <td class="nowrap"><a href="#">{name}</a></td>
          <td>
            {why}
            <span :if={days} class="tag warning">{days} days</span>
            <span class="sub small">{detail}</span>
          </td>
          <td class="shrink"><button class="btn sm secondary">Review</button></td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Activities, compact</h2>
  <p>
    The compact size, for long lists people scan rather than read. The kind as a marker, "Draft"
    only when it applies, primary or secondary beside the hours, D4H's other tags outlined, and
    the tracking number as text.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="compact striped">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="shrink" aria-sort="descending">
            <a href="#">Date<span class="sort">↓</span></a>
          </th>
          <th class="shrink">Kind</th>
          <th>Title</th>
          <th class="num">Attended</th>
          <th class="num">Hours</th>
          <th>Tags</th>
          <th class="shrink">Number</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr :for={a <- activities()}>
          <td class="nowrap">{a.date}</td>
          <td>
            <span class={["kind", a.kind]}>{a.kind |> Atom.to_string() |> String.capitalize()}</span>
          </td>
          <td><a href="#">{a.title}</a> <span :if={a.draft} class="tag">Draft</span></td>
          <td class="num">{a.count}</td>
          <td class="num">
            <span :if={a.hours_type} class="muted">{a.hours_type}</span> {a.hours}
          </td>
          <td>
            <span class="tags">
              <span :for={t <- a.tags} class="tag outline">{t}</span>
            </span>
          </td>
          <td class="mono">{a.number}</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</.shell>
